      "simulation": {
        "ada": "reachable zones report a defined non-compliance fraction in [0,1]; a deliberate 2 ft (<36 in) pinch exists in zone B between tsaw (y8-10 ft) and wjet (y12-14 ft) at x42-45.6 ft on the bridge->exitB path, so ADA non-compliance must be > 0 in at least one reachable zone.",
        "egress": "zone C (no exit) is unreachable and EXCLUDED from the building aggregate; zones A and B each seed egress from their exterior exit (and the bridge) and report a defined egress in [0,1].",
        "aggregateExcludesUnreachable": true,
        "mosa": "the generalized 3-objective driver returns a non-empty Pareto front whose members are mutually non-dominated, deterministic across repeated runs at a fixed seed.",
        "frontier": "presentFront returns a defined knee and per-objective best for the front."
      }
    },
    "notes": {
      "finding": "The app (v1 import wizard) and the v2 stack use INCOMPATIBLE formats; this file drives ONLY the v2 pipeline. See testcase/diagnostic/README.md and diagnostic-project.app.json for the degraded app fixture and the lost-in-translation list.",
      "geometry": "Room = 60x40 ft with a 15x12 ft SE notch (area 2220 ft2). Interior vertical wall at x=30 ft splits left/right; a bridge door connects zones A and B. A horizontal wall at y=25 ft seals off zone C (bottom-left, 450 ft2) with NO door -> unreachable.",
      "amenities": "weld->fireExt (8.15 ft < 30) SATISFIED; laser->fireExt (18.2 < 30) SATISFIED; wjet->eyewash (41.9 < 55) SATISFIED; grind->eyewash (59.0 > 55) VIOLATED. Distances are straight-line center-to-center (ANSI Z358.1 / NFPA 10 are travel distances; true travel is longer, so the violation is conservative). Unsatisfiable links (no amenity of that type placed, e.g. dustCollection/fumeHood/flammablesCabinet) are reported as UNSATISFIABLE, not failures.",
      "adaEgress": "DELIBERATE DEFECTS: (1) ADA pinch — tsaw and wjet leave a 2 ft vertical gap (<36 in) across the bridge->exitB corridor. (2) Egress — zone C has no exit (unreachable); the pinch also narrows B's egress path. The simulations should surface non-zero ADA non-compliance and exclude C from the aggregate.",
      "provenanceHazards": "Hazard flags, clearance zones, amenity links, power, and occupancy are copied verbatim from v2/machine-library.json (provenance-tagged there)."
    }
